ref: WI-995). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes.","+- 2026-11-07 — refresh under approval. Copied: low-level-requirements.toml (re-attested: LLR-143); test-cases.toml (re-attested: TC-137). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-1002\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":1094,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1094,"newLines":10,"lines":[" approved = [\"LLR-367\", \"TC-413\", \"TC-414\", \"TC-415\", \"TC-416\", \"TC-417\", \"TC-418\", \"TC-419\", \"TC-420\"]"," reattested = []"," copied = [\"docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\", \"docs/test/test-cases.toml\"]","+","+[[act]]","+seq = 179","+date = \"2026-11-07\"","+approved = []","+reattested = [\"LLR-143\", \"TC-137\"]","+copied = [\"docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\", \"docs/test/test-cases.toml\"]"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-1002\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":1417,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1417,"newLines":7,"lines":[" title = \"Plain-launch drive loop (claim->build->integrate)\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/dispatch.py\""," code_symbol = \"run/_stop_run\"","-detail = \"\"\"The scheduling front end a plain agent_loop.py launch runs, serial at lanes=1 (the lanes dial admits more lanes at once; each lane's mechanics are LLR-150's): each cycle re-derives the ready frontier (schedule.frontier), stops claiming under the tracked pause (a parked or finished lane still resumes and merges, and the run exits 8 once nothing is in flight), refuses on a dirty trunk at the cycle top while no lane is live (a change confined to agent_common.OWNER_ONLY_PATHS, the owner's scratchpad, is not dirt), resumes a parked claimed branch else claims the next queued WI in build order (integrate.claim, branch name check-ref-format-validated), launches one worker session on the claimed branch's worktree (agent_loop.py --worktree --wi with the session dials forwarded), merges each finished branch through the serial merge slot (integrate.integrate) counting the WIs merged, and stops loudly on any composed refusal once the live lanes drain - a stall aborts, an empty frontier drains to exit 0. A NEEDS-HUMAN worker does not stop the run: its lane hands back (the WI closes partial and merges) and the run drives on; an active/ directory with no branch ref is residue, not a refusal. The session-config preflight applies only when work needs a worker. Never pushes.\"\"\"","+detail = \"\"\"The scheduling front end a plain agent_loop.py launch runs, serial at lanes=1 (the lanes dial admits more lanes at once; each lane's mechanics are LLR-150's): each cycle re-derives the ready frontier (schedule.frontier), stops claiming under the tracked pause (a parked or finished lane still resumes and merges, and the run exits 8 once nothing is in flight), refuses on a dirty trunk at the cycle top while no lane is live (a change confined to agent_common.OWNER_ONLY_PATHS, the owner's scratchpad, is not dirt), resumes a parked claimed branch else claims the next queued WI in build order (integrate.claim, branch name check-ref-format-validated), launches one worker session on the claimed branch's worktree (agent_loop.py --worktree --wi with the session dials forwarded), merges each finished branch through the serial merge slot (integrate.integrate) counting the WIs merged, and stops loudly on any composed refusal once the live lanes drain - a stall aborts, an empty frontier drains to exit 0. A NEEDS-HUMAN worker does not stop the run: its lane hands back (the WI closes partial and merges) and the run drives on; an active/ directory with no branch ref is residue, not a refusal. A parked claimed branch whose claimed row reads blocked in the shared schedule is left out of resume: it launches no worker, keeps its claim, and the next ready row is claimed; the excluded lane does not count as a stall. A parked lane whose claimed row reads anything else resumes as before. The session-config preflight applies only when work needs a worker. Never pushes.\"\"\""," rationale = \"\"\"Ordering only, no new authority: every refusal stays where it already lives, and the driver is ~400 lines of composition against the 4,042-line dispatcher it replaces.\"\"\""," test_refs = \"(see TC-137)\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-1002\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":1348,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1348,"newLines":7,"lines":[" [test.TC-137]"," verifies = [\"SR-026\", \"LLR-143\"]"," level = \"Unit\"","-method = \"\"\"Run the drive suite: an unwired agent command refuses before any claim while an empty queue still drains to exit 0; a refusing claim rung, a dirty trunk and a red refresh bar each stop the run by name, while a claim directory with no branch ref does not stop it and a trunk whose only change is confined to the owner's scratchpad (agent_common.OWNER_ONLY_PATHS) is not dirty and the parked lane resumes; the tracked pause appearing mid-run stops the next claim while the lane in flight merges, exiting 8; a NEEDS-HUMAN worker hands its lane back as a partial close that merges, and the run drives on to exit 0; a DONE-reporting worker that finishes nothing trips the stall guard; and two end-to-end runs against the real bar prove the green path (claim->build->merge->drained banner) and the red path (the refresh bar red on the branch, nothing merged, the claimed branch left in place with no refresh attestation). The plain agent_loop.py launch enters the drive mode as a subprocess.\"\"\"","+method = \"\"\"Run the drive suite: an unwired agent command refuses before any claim while an empty queue still drains to exit 0; a refusing claim rung, a dirty trunk and a red refresh bar each stop the run by name, while a claim directory with no branch ref does not stop it and a trunk whose only change is confined to the owner's scratchpad (agent_common.OWNER_ONLY_PATHS) is not dirty and the parked lane resumes; the tracked pause appearing mid-run stops the next claim while the lane in flight merges, exiting 8; a NEEDS-HUMAN worker hands its lane back as a partial close that merges, and the run drives on to exit 0; a DONE-reporting worker that finishes nothing trips the stall guard; and two end-to-end runs against the real bar prove the green path (claim->build->merge->drained banner) and the red path (the refresh bar red on the branch, nothing merged, the claimed branch left in place with no refresh attestation). The plain agent_loop.py launch enters the drive mode as a subprocess. A parked lane whose claimed row reads blocked, beside a ready row, draws no worker and keeps its claim while the run claims and merges the ready row and ends without a stall; the same lane citing a ruled item resumes first.\"\"\""," tier = \"Full\""," expected = \"Satisfies SR-026 AcceptanceCriteria\""," automated = \"Yes\""]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-1002\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-1002\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-1002\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-1002\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01F88FtphTXbgYtXVWnms3CD","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
